# node-vitest adapter manifest — the DATA fields of the generic Node/TS
# StackAdapter. Code fields (detect/install/discover/probe/run/coverage) stay in
# src/adapters/node-vitest/index.ts; auditRules stays TS (jsAuditRules). Anything
# declared here overrides via manifestFields('node-vitest'). Partial by design.
# guidance/patterns are kind-independent — both unit and e2e blocks are the SAME
# text, reproducing the TS's kind-agnostic behavior byte-for-byte.

adapter node-vitest
  command typecheck = npx tsc --noEmit
  command lint = true
  command test-unit = npx vitest run
  command test-e2e = true
  command coverage = npx vitest run --coverage --coverage.reporter=json-summary
  patterns unit = node-unit-patterns.md
  patterns e2e = node-unit-patterns.md
  guidance unit:
    (vitest, plain TS) place the test next to its source as src/<name>.test.ts. ALWAYS `import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'` (no globals). Import the exported functions and assert concrete values; cover happy paths, edge cases, and error paths. No DOM, no framework. Use only the ground-truth exports.
  guidance e2e:
    (vitest, plain TS) place the test next to its source as src/<name>.test.ts. ALWAYS `import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest'` (no globals). Import the exported functions and assert concrete values; cover happy paths, edge cases, and error paths. No DOM, no framework. Use only the ground-truth exports.
